\par\par \b \uc2 Boeing Furloughs Engineer, Office Staff Amid Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sharon Terlep \par \uc2 312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is furloughing tens of thousands of white-collar employees in an effort to cut costs and avoid a credit-ratings cut amid a strike by its largest union.\par \par \uc2 The jet maker will furlough affected employees for one week out of every four weeks for the duration of the walkout, Chief Executive \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  wrote in a memo to employees Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The strike, which has halted production of the 737 and other jets, could cost the manufacturer some $500 million a week, according to one analyst estimate. The company's operations had been burning about $1 billion a month before the strike. Credit-ratings firms warned they may downgrade \uc2 Boeing\uc2  if the strike drags on. Ratings firms \uc2 Moody's\uc2  and \uc2 Fitch\uc2  both rate \uc2 Boeing\uc2  one notch above junk status.\par \par \uc2 "While this is a tough decision that impacts everybody, it is in an effort to preserve our long-term future and help us navigate through this very difficult time," said Ortberg, who added that he and his executive team will take a pay cut for the duration of the strike.\par \par \uc2 The executives' pay will be cut by 25%, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  earlier this week said it would freeze hiring and pay increases, among other cost-cutting measures.\par \par \uc2 A union representing some 17,000 \uc2 Boeing\uc2  engineers -- about 10% of the overall workforce -- said its contract with the company prohibits furloughs and, in the case of layoffs, requires company payouts to idled workers. Federal law requires employers of a certain size to give 60 days' notice to workers when conducting big layoffs, with some exceptions.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for the union, known as Speea, said the company had not approached it as of Wednesday to discuss either furloughs or layoffs.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's 33,000-member machinist's union walked out Friday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240919ek9j0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
