\par\par \uc2 REVIEW & OUTLOOK (Editorial)\par \b \uc2 Machinists Strike While \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Is Weak\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A14\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Talk about a rough takeoff. A month into his new job, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  CEO \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2  is having to steer through choppy labor negotiations amid a financial squeeze. On Friday some 33,000 \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  plants in Seattle and Portland voted to strike after rejecting a new contract endorsed by their union leaders.\par \par \uc2 The contract would have provided an average 25% raise over four years, with bigger increases in minimum pay for varying job classifications. An aviation maintenance technician and inspector would start at $35 an hour -- up from the current $24 -- and max out at $55.97. The lowest rank would begin at $20 -- up from $15 -- and top out at $26.32.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  also agreed to kick in $4,160 more a year to employee 401(k)s, on top of $5,200 in employer matches and other contributions. The contract also reduced worker health premiums and boosted prescription drug benefits. This seems like a generous offer at a time that many employers are paring benefits.\par \par \uc2 But workers want larger raises to make up for inflation over the past few years, as well as restoration of defined-benefit pensions that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  scrapped a decade ago because of their ballooning costs.\par \par \uc2 Trouble is, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is flying into financial headwinds owing to problems of its own making. It has been required by the government to ground planes after crashes of its 737 Max in 2018 and 2019 and slow production after a mid-flight panel blowout in January. A \uc2 National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  review this year found myriad production problems.\par \par \uc2 The company has paid $2.5 billion to settle claims by the Justice Department and airlines over its 737 Max. Add billions of dollars in cost overruns on fixed-price defense and space contracts, and the U.S. aerospace giant has lost more than $25 billion over the last six years, with $12 billion in debt coming due over the next two years. Buckle up, shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  warned Friday of a credit-rating downgrade to junk if the strike drags on, which would make it harder to refinance maturing debt. Its 2008 strike cost the company $100 million a day in revenue. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and \uc2 Airbus\uc2  have a duopoly in large airplane manufacturing, but \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is losing market share and China's state-backed Comac is wooing airlines in lower-income countries. Losing contracts won't help \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 The strike vindicates \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's decision to shift some production in 2011 to a non-union factory in North Charleston, S.C., and could spur it to make more future planes there. Manufacturing employment in the Seattle metro region has fallen by 19,300 over the last decade while increasing by 10,200 around North Charleston.\par \par \uc2 Unhelpful as usual, the White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  on Friday said \uc2 Boeing\uc2  needs to "negotiate in good faith and work towards an agreement that gives employees benefits that they deserve." This suggests the Administration thinks the company is short-changing workers, which will embolden the rank-and-file to strike for more than \uc2 Boeing\uc2  can feasibly offer.\par \par \uc2 Step back, and the \uc2 Boeing\uc2  strike is an advertisement for right-to-work states where workers aren't compelled to join unions. Average manufacturing wages have grown three times faster in South Carolina than in Washington state in the last decade. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  workers would do better in the long run if they moved to South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 (See related letters: "Letters to the Editor: Why the Machinists at \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Are on Strike" -- WSJ Sept. 20, 2024)\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240917ek9h0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
