\par\par \b \uc2 EXCHANGE --- The Score / The Business Week in 6 Stocks: Boeing Workers Strike, Norfolk Ousts Its CEO\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francesca Fontana \par \uc2 544 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BOEING\par \par \uc2 BA -3.7%\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  has been grounded by a labor dispute. Its biggest labor union went on strike Friday, halting production of its bestselling jets and dealing the latest blow to the struggling aerospace giant. Thousands of machinists walked off the job shortly after midnight Pacific time after overwhelmingly rejecting a labor deal struck Sunday morning between the union's leaders and \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's executives. The contract offered 25% wage increases over four years. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is working on a new contract offer to address the union's concerns, finance chief \uc2 Brian West\uc2  told an investor conference Friday. The strike will "jeopardize our recovery," he said, adding that the company is now conserving as much cash as possible. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  shares fell 3.7% Friday.\par \par \uc2 ORACLE\par \par \uc2 ORCL +11%\par \par \uc2 The cloud-software provider on Monday posted better-than-expected quarterly results, as its partnership with artificial-intelligence chip maker \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  boosted revenue. The company has emerged as an attractive cloud-computing provider for AI developers such as \uc2 OpenAI\uc2 , sending its long-stagnant stock to new heights. On Thursday, \uc2 Oracle\uc2  unveiled unexpectedly strong financial targets at its annual user conference. \uc2 Oracle\uc2  shares rallied 11% Tuesday and were up 14% for the week.\par \par \uc2 UNDER ARMOUR\par \par \uc2 UAA -8.7%\par \par \uc2 The sportswear retailer on Monday lowered its outlook for fiscal 2025, saying it expects to double its restructuring costs as it closes a distribution facility and lays off more workers. Since Chief Executive \uc2 Kevin Plank\uc2  returned to the top job earlier this year, the company has been working on a turnaround. The latest cost-cutting actions came after the company posted a surprise quarterly adjusted profit amid slumping sales last month. \uc2 Under Armour\uc2  shares dropped 8.7% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 NORFOLK SOUTHERN\par \par \uc2 NSC -1.4%\par \par \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2 's board terminated Chief Executive \uc2 Alan Shaw\uc2  after discovering he had a consensual relationship with the company's top lawyer. The chief legal officer, \uc2 Nabanita Nag\uc2 , was also fired, the railroad said Wednesday. A three-decade veteran of the company, Shaw will be succeeded by Chief Financial Officer \uc2 Mark George\uc2 . Activist investor \uc2 Ancora Holdings\uc2  caught wind of the board's investigation before it was public, The Wall Street Journal reported. Norfolk shares fell 1.4% Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 LUV -1.6%\par \par \uc2 Executive Chairman \uc2 Gary Kelly\uc2  will step down next year as Southwest faces pressure from \uc2 Elliott Investment Management\uc2  to overhaul its leadership and business strategy. Six other Southwest directors intend to retire in November. The company said it would appoint four new directors in the near future and would consider filling as many as three of those spots with candidates from the slate Elliott put forward last month. \uc2 Southwest Airlines\uc2  shares fell 1.6% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ALLY FINANCIAL\par \par \uc2 ALLY\uc2  -18%\par \par \uc2 Ally\uc2 's customers are struggling with the high cost of living, inflation and a weakening labor market, Chief Financial Officer \uc2 Russ Hutchinson\uc2  said Tuesday. He pointed to the bank's auto loans as a key problem area for the bank, and said that \uc2 Ally\uc2  will likely have to increase loan-loss reserves. In July and August, delinquencies increased and the bank's net charge-off rate was above expectations, he said. \uc2 Ally\uc2  shares plummeted 18% Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240914ek9e0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
