\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 PwC\uc2  to Lay Off 1,800 As New U.S. Leader Revamps Operations\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mark Maurer \par \uc2 367 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PricewaterhouseCoopers\uc2 's U.S. unit is laying off about 1,800 workers, its first formal layoffs since 2009, and restructuring its products and technology group to simplify operations and address declining demand for certain advisory services.\par \par \uc2 The Big Four accounting firm is in the process of cutting employees in the U.S. and elsewhere, primarily in its U.S. advisory and products and technology operations, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 The cuts, about half of which are offshore, span employees ranging from associates to managing directors and include business services, audit and tax, the people said.\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  plans to notify those affected, roughly 2.5% of the workforce at the U.S. unit, in October, the people said.\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  announced the plans Wednesday in a memo to U.S. staff reviewed by The Wall Street Journal. "There will be an element of resource action that will impact a relatively small proportion of our people, something that is never easy," Paul Griggs, \uc2 PwC\uc2 's U.S. leader, said in the memo.\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2  plans to restructure its products and technology teams to further embed them in individual business lines and streamline processes in business services, Griggs said.\par \par \uc2 The moves come after Griggs began as U.S. leader in May. He launched a structural overhaul that took effect in July, shifting the 75,000-person U.S. unit back to three business lines from two. Tax returned to being a separate U.S. business in July. The firm in 2021 had combined tax-reporting and accounting into one unit, with remaining revenue stemming from consulting solutions, which included tax consulting.\par \par \uc2 "To remain competitive and position our business for the future, we are continuing to transform areas of our firm and are aligning our workforce to better support our strategy, including attracting and moving the right talent and skill sets to the areas where we need them most," Tim Grady, \uc2 PwC\uc2 's U.S. chief operating officer, said.\par \par \uc2 PwC\uc2 's products and technologies are aimed at addressing a range of corporate challenges, including managing risks around supply chains, data privacy and regulations.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240912ek9c00010\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
