\par\par \b \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  Chief Has Tall Order: Calming an Anxious Workforce\b0\par\par\uc2 By Heather Haddon \par \uc2 869 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Incoming \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Brian Niccol\uc2  partook in a ceremonial "first sip" of coffee Monday as he reported for his first day of work. For \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees, it is another change to digest.\par \par \uc2 The coffee chain's board of directors, investors and longtime leader \uc2 Howard Schultz\uc2  have embraced Niccol since his hiring last month, praising the former \uc2 Chipotle Mexican Grill\uc2  CEO as the best possible choice to turn around \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's operations and restore its brand after a turbulent few years.\par \par \uc2 At the company's Seattle headquarters and across its U.S. cafes, the reception is more mixed. Some \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers said the rapid turnover in the CEO role -- Niccol will be the company's fourth in less than three years -- is fatiguing. Many said they were hopeful that Niccol's restaurant-industry experience would lead to improvements, though some felt jarred by former CEO \uc2 Laxman Narasimhan\uc2 's abrupt August ouster, a year and a half into the job.\par \par \uc2 Niccol plans to host a town hall Tuesday. This week he will also meet with baristas in cafes and employees at headquarters, and start assessing the company's challenges and opportunities.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  for years has struggled with cafe operations, where orders for often-complex drinks have frequently overwhelmed baristas and created long lines of frustrated customers. Snarled stores and rising prices have contributed to employee turnover and declining traffic, pressuring the company's results.\par \par \uc2 Over the past five years, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  shares have increased by about 2%, while the S&P 500 stock index has gained around 82%. In recent months, the company has faced activist investors and public criticism from Schultz over its operations.\par \par \uc2 "Time is of the essence," wrote \uc2 Rachel Ruggeri\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's chief financial officer and interim CEO, in a letter to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  employees Monday as she officially handed the role to Niccol.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's recent relations with workers have often been uneasy. Three years ago, baristas, frustrated with pay and working conditions, began unionizing. In March 2022, \uc2 Kevin Johnson\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's CEO at the time, stepped down and was succeeded by Schultz. Taking over for a third stint as CEO, Schultz reinvested in stores, raised wages for baristas and helped position a permanent successor.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  picked former \uc2 Reckitt Benckiser Group\uc2  CEO Narasimhan, who underwent a six-month training that included working as a barista. But the company's challenges deepened, with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  in April cutting its sales outlook for the second time this year.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street was enthused last month when \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  poached Niccol from Chipotle, bringing to \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  restaurant-operations chops that Narasimhan lacked, and turnaround experience. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's shares have gained around 20% since his hiring was announced.\par \par \uc2 Internal reactions at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  have been more complicated, according to store managers, corporate workers and others with the chain, which prizes ritual and tradition. Some employees said they feel like they have navigated years of shifting executive-office priorities and personalities, from Narasimhan's focus on supply chain to Schultz's backing of an olive oil-infused coffee.\par \par \uc2 Manny Paz, a district manager from Southern California, said Niccol introduced himself when he visited Paz's store during a recent Pumpkin Spice Latte promotion. Niccol chatted with the baristas and sampled one of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 's signature drinks.\par \par \uc2 "He's a genuine and curious individual," Paz said.\par \par \uc2 Some workers were skeptical of the hybrid-work arrangement that allows Niccol to commute to Seattle on a company jet and establish an office near his Southern California home. Narasimhan had moved to Seattle from London to take the CEO position, and the chain expects Seattle-based corporate employees to generally work from headquarters three days a week.\par \par \uc2 Several \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  store managers said they wished Ruggeri, the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  financial chief, would become the next CEO, noting her long tenure and candor with employees. Others wished they could have said goodbye to Narasimhan, who regularly convened informal chats with employees.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said it has sought to listen to and address workers' concerns about the abrupt CEO transition, and it established a way for employees to share their gratitude to Narasimhan.\par \par \uc2 "We look forward to the fresh ideas that Brian will bring to our business," \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Some \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  alumni said that despite the tumult, a shake-up was merited after a spate of lackluster performance.\par \par \uc2 "Things were really bleak," said Major Cohen, a former chain project manager who retired in 2020 after 25 years at the company.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  didn't make Niccol available for an interview. He informed Chipotle on Aug. 12 of his decision to step down, and he has met with Starbucks's U.S. leaders and visited dozens of cafes since, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Niccol, 50 years old, helped turn Chipotle into an industry powerhouse after it was laid low by food-safety problems. Niccol said last month that he was energized by the opportunity to spur growth at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and make improvements for customers and employees.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  is moving ahead negotiating with Workers United, the union that has organized bargaining units at 475 of the chain's 9,950 U.S. stores as of last month. The company and the union said they have made progress on contract term.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich446\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6690
