\par\par \b \uc2 Biden Set to Halt U.S. Steel Deal, Amid Threat of Plant Closings\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bob Tita \par \uc2 891 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 's chief executive said the company would close steel mills if its planned sale to \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  collapses, as the Biden administration is moving closer to blocking the deal.\par \par \uc2 CEO \uc2 David Burritt\uc2  said the nearly $3 billion that Japan-based \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  has pledged to invest in the Pittsburgh company's older mills is critical to keeping them competitive and maintaining workers' jobs.\par \par \uc2 "We wouldn't do that if the deal falls through," Burritt said in an interview. "I don't have the money."\par \par \uc2 He also said the company would likely move its headquarters out of Pittsburgh if the deal fails.\par \par \uc2 President Biden, who earlier this year said that \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  should remain domestically owned and operated, is planning to block the deal, though the final signoff hasn't yet happened, according to a person familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Burritt's dour outlook for the storied steelmaker came after Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the same position Monday. Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and several members of Congress have similarly lined up against the $14.1 billion deal, which the \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union also opposes.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  shares fell 17% Wednesday to $29.38 after the initial reports that Biden would scuttle the deal. \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  and \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  said they haven't received any update or executive order related to the national-security review.\par \par \uc2 "We continue to stand by the fact that there are no national-security issues associated with this transaction, as Japan is one of our most staunch allies," \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  said. \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  said its planned investments would put \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  and the American steel industry on stronger footing.\par \par \uc2 Burritt has largely refrained from talking publicly about the deal since it was announced in December following a monthslong bidding process. He said in the interview that \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  would bring investment and the latest steelmaking technology to \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 's older mills in Gary, Ind., and its Mon Valley Works near Pittsburgh, and described the opposition as "puzzling and confusing."\par \par \uc2 For months, the Japanese steelmaker has been courting elected officials and union leaders to build support for its purchase and investment commitments.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Steelworkers\uc2  union said Burritt's threats to close mills were an attempt to shift attention away from what it called his bad management of the company and an ill-conceived merger with \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 . The union said the deal would allow \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  to gut \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 's operations to benefit its steel mills in Japan.\par \par \uc2 "His reckless statements and mismanagement are the only true obstacles to \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  remaining a sustainable steel company," the union said.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  executives have said they are interested in acquiring \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 's operations to expand into the U.S., a market where the company has had a limited presence.\par \par \uc2 The deal has been under a national-security review by the \uc2 Committee on Foreign Investment in the U.S.\uc2 , which can recommend that the president block a potential deal. The Justice Department also is conducting an antitrust review of the transaction.\par \par \uc2 The White House has been weighing the political aspects of the potential \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  sale, with Pennsylvania a battleground state in the coming presidential election. Biden has sought to broaden the definition of national security to include safeguarding the domestic economy and signed an executive order that pushed \uc2 Cfius\uc2  to protect the U.S. industrial base beyond military production.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2 , the world's fourth largest steel producer by tonnage, last week pledged to nearly double its investment commitment for \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 's older mills to $2.7 billion over the coming years. The company also has said it would refrain from layoffs of hourly workers through 2026.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  on Wednesday released its corporate governance blueprint for \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2 , which includes maintaining U.S. citizens in key management positions at the company.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  since 2020 has idled portions of its mills near Detroit and St. Louis, shrinking its hourly unionized workforce by about 4,000 to roughly 10,000 workers. The company canceled an upgrade to the Mon Valley plant in 2021 when it was in the process of purchasing a new steel mill in Arkansas, staffed by nonunion workers. The company is doubling the production capacity of that mill to 6 million tons of steel annually.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  and \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  both make most of their steel from iron ore. Without \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  as a corporate parent, \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  would continue to shift more production to less capital-intensive operations like the Arkansas mill that produces new steel from melting scrap, Burritt said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  CEO said the expanded Arkansas mill would allow the company to close Mon Valley, its last steelmaking operation in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 "If that mill won't make it to the next decade, why would we stay there?" he said. With more of the company's production shifting to the South, he said \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  would likely look to move its headquarters to the region as well.\par \par \uc2 Nippon Steel\uc2  executives have said that under their ownership, \uc2 U.S. Steel\uc2  would maintain its headquarters in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Andrew Restuccia contributed to this article.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw262\pich466\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3930\pichgoal6990
