\par\par \b \uc2 AT&T\uc2  Strike in Southeast Drags On As Union Rejects Mediation Process\b0\par\par\uc2 By Drew FitzGerald \par \uc2 557 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 September 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 The Communications Workers of America withdrew from federal mediation with AT&T on Saturday. A Business & Finance article on Wednesday about a strike at AT&T incorrectly said the union withdrew Monday.\par \par \uc2 (WSJ Sept. 5, 2024)\par \par \uc2 (END)\par \par \uc2 A strike by more than 15,000 \uc2 AT&T\uc2  workers in the Southeast is stretching into a third week after a federal mediation process to end the standoff broke down.\par \par \uc2 Wireline technicians, customer-service representatives and other workers across nine states walked off the job Aug. 16 after the telecom giant failed to reach an agreement with \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2  negotiators on a new contract. The union agreed last week to \uc2 AT&T\uc2 's proposal to join talks under the \uc2 Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service\uc2  but said Monday that it withdrew.\par \par \uc2 Richard Honeycutt\uc2 , CWA District 3 vice president, said the telecom giant used the mediation process as another delaying tactic and hadn't sent representatives empowered to effectively negotiate.\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 AT&T\uc2  spokesman said the withdrawal surprised the company. "Regardless of whether a neutral third-party is present, progress will not be made without a willingness to compromise," the company said. The now-expired contract covers more than 15,000 employees.\par \par \uc2 The Dallas company's union-represented workforce is spread across multiple regions with staggered contract lengths, so the company is unlikely to face a nationwide work stoppage. The company's Southeastern workers -- who work in Alabama, Florida, Georgia, Kentucky, Louisiana, Mississippi, North Carolina, South Carolina and Tennessee -- also went on strike in 2019 for less than a week.\par \par \uc2 Workers in the region have complained of high healthcare costs and a tiered-title system that burdens junior employees with heavy, unpredictable workloads. But the talks this year have snagged on the negotiating process itself.\par \par \uc2 The union last month filed an unfair labor practice complaint with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  that accused the company of bargaining in bad faith. \uc2 AT&T\uc2  said it is focused on reaching a fair and competitive agreement.\par \par \uc2 AT&T\uc2  has so far used other workers to handle customer calls and installations, though it relies more heavily than some rivals on union labor nationwide. About 42% of its 149,000 workers were represented by a union as of January, compared with about 24% at rival \uc2 Verizon Communications\uc2 , according to securities filings. \uc2 T-Mobile US\uc2  doesn't have a unionized workforce.\par \par \uc2 More than 36,000 \uc2 Verizon\uc2  workers struck for nearly seven weeks before the two sides reached an agreement in 2016. About 1,700 workers for New England telecom company \uc2 FairPoint\uc2  stayed on strike for 18 weeks into early 2015.\par \par \uc2 Phone and cable companies have pared their in-house labor in recent years and relied on more contractors for construction, installation and repair work. But demand for network builders of all stripes is expected to surge in the coming years once a $42.5 billion broadband deployment program starts doling out contracts.\par \par \uc2 The federal internet construction project, launched under President Biden's 2021 infrastructure law, is designed to connect the millions of American households that lack affordable broadband service through state-run plans. Some states have promoted union-friendly rules for project grants, though the program's lengthy planning process means most new construction isn't expected to start until 2026.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240904ek940003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
