\par\par \b \uc2 Amazon Loses Bid To Overturn Workers' Unionization Victory\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sebastian Herrera \par \uc2 411 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal labor agency has denied \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 's request to overturn the results of a 2022 election in which workers voted to unionize a Staten Island, N.Y., warehouse.\par \par \uc2 A three-member panel from the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  denied Amazon's appeal, according to an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  filing Thursday. Amazon had appealed an earlier decision by a federal labor official that also denied the company's request to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 The decision means Amazon has essentially run out of options to reject the election results through the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  and will likely have to sue the agency if it seeks to present its arguments in court.\par \par \uc2 As it has gone through the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  appeals process, Amazon and the union haven't had serious negotiations about a labor contract.\par \par \uc2 An Amazon spokeswoman said the company plans to challenge the latest ruling.\par \par \uc2 "We believe today's decision will be overturned when it's reviewed by an unbiased court," she said.\par \par \uc2 Chris Smalls, who has led Amazon unionization efforts on Staten Island, wrote in an X post on Thursday that Amazon "needs to stop wasting its time and money and come to the Table!"\par \par \uc2 Amazon shares, which have risen more than 13% so far this year, closed up less than 1% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Amazon has said the union and \uc2 NLRB\uc2  regional office that oversaw the vote created an unfair playing field for the election. It also took issue with the legal actions the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  took against the company during the election.\par \par \uc2 Amazon workers voted to unionize the large warehouse on Staten Island in 2022, creating the first unionized group in the company's history. Workers haven't unionized other facilities.\par \par \uc2 The Amazon Labor Union, the New York organization that has represented the Staten Island unionized employees, recently voted to join the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , one of America's most prominent labor organizations. The Amazon union had been struggling to survive.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  are organizing Amazon workers and have focused on delivery drivers.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a regional director for the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said that Amazon is a joint employer of subcontracted drivers who deliver packages for the company from Palmdale, Calif. That ruling could serve as a proxy for how the agency views Amazon's relationship with drivers.\par \par \uc2 The company has argued that drivers who are contracted to deliver its packages through third-party companies aren't its employees but "delivery service partners."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240830ek8u0001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
