\par\par \b \uc2 FTC\uc2 , Grocery Giants Square Off --- Antitrust trial opens in government's bid to halt Albertsons, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  from merging\b0\par\par\uc2 By Dave Michaels \par \uc2 847 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PORTLAND, Ore. -- \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  went to court Monday to defend the largest supermarket merger in history from antitrust enforcers who say it would create a supermarket colossus that could raise prices on consumers and stifle wage increases for workers.\par \par \uc2 A federal court in Oregon will consider over the next two weeks whether to grant the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2 's request to block the $20 billion merger from closing. Stores owned by \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  compete against one another in thousands of local markets, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  says. The rivalry puts a ceiling on food prices, and eliminating it would free \uc2 Kroger\uc2  to raise them, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2 , which in 2022 struck the deal to purchase \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 , says it needs to get bigger to compete with rivals such as \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco\uc2  that lure customers with lower prices than traditional supermarkets have been able to offer. \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's prices today are 10% to 12% lower than \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 ', the food retailer's lawyer told the court Monday. \uc2 Kroger\uc2  says it would invest $1 billion to lower prices at the \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  stores.\par \par \uc2 The trial comes as U.S. consumers have grappled over the past several years with higher rates of food inflation and both presidential candidates have vowed to bring them down. Prices for food at home were 26% higher in July than they were at the end of 2019, whereas prices for goods excluding food and energy were up 14%.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates in the presidential election, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , have teed off on rising food prices. Harris has effectively blamed supermarkets for driving up food prices, citing corporate greed, and called for a ban on price gouging. Trump has blamed regulation and Biden administration policies for fueling and failing to control inflation.\par \par \uc2 "This lawsuit is part of an effort aimed at helping Americans feed their families," \uc2 FTC\uc2  attorney Susan Musser said Monday in her opening argument to the court. "Stopping a multibillion-dollar deal will keep in place bigger competition that acts as a check on rising grocery prices and furthers improvements in quality and innovation."\par \par \uc2 Courts can block mergers that may lead to a substantial loss of competition. Like in most merger trials, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  and \uc2 Kroger\uc2  will offer the court competing expert witnesses who will try to predict the risk of that outcome.\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2 , which would operate more than 4,000 stores if the deal closes, says the merger would create a nationwide footprint of stores that would allow it to compete more effectively with \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , \uc2 Costco\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon.com\uc2 . The \uc2 FTC\uc2  is improperly fixated on one-stop-shop supermarkets rather than considering how \uc2 Costco\uc2 , Trader Joe's and newer entrants such as \uc2 Aldi\uc2  will restrain \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's ability to raise prices, \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's lawyers say.\par \par \uc2 "We are really, really focused on \uc2 Walmart\uc2 ," \uc2 Kroger\uc2  attorney Matthew Wolf said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2 's antitrust enforcers "refuse to recognize the tectonic shift that has occurred in the grocery industry over the last 20 years, refusing to acknowledge that unless traditional grocers act, the dominance of \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and their ilk will only grow," Wolf said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2  says the merger would result in excessive concentration in over 1,900 local markets across the country, far more than what the companies have acknowledged. While both companies set prices with an eye to what \uc2 Walmart\uc2  charges, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  are often in direct competition with one another in many markets, according to the \uc2 FTC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  have acknowledged their stores overlap in many markets and have agreed to sell off 579 stores to \uc2 C&S Wholesale Grocers\uc2 . C&S supplies products to retailers across the country but operates relatively few stores on its own.\par \par \uc2 Most of the divested assets would be \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  stores in the West. New Hampshire-based C&S has said it is prepared to invest in those stores and make them viable competitors to \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and others.\par \par \uc2 Selling stores to C&S won't cure the deal's problems, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 C&S has a poor record of running stores and has sold or closed hundreds of them over the past two decades, according to the \uc2 FTC\uc2 . C&S expects sales to fall at the stores it acquires as it rebrands many of them and updates their layout and product mix, \uc2 FTC\uc2  attorney Laura Hall told the court Monday. Those stores won't recapture their current level of profitability for 11 years, Hall said.\par \par \uc2 In addition to potentially fueling higher prices, the merger would harm union workers' bargaining power, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  alleges. Employees couldn't credibly threaten to join a rival supermarket's union workforce if their employer refused to raise pay or benefits, enforcers say.\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2  says the union would be more powerful when it has to negotiate with only one employer.\par \par \uc2 In the hearing that began Monday, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  wants U.S. District Judge Adrienne Nelson to issue a preliminary injunction that would stop the companies from closing their deal.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240827ek8r0001p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
