\par\par \b \uc2 Cisco\uc2  to Slash 7% of Global Workforce --- IT company expects restructuring plan to cost up to $1 billion; results beat forecast\b0\par\par\uc2 By Denny Jacob \par \uc2 307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cisco Systems\uc2  unveiled a restructuring plan that will eliminate 7% of its global workforce, citing a need to cut costs and invest in growth areas.\par \par \uc2 The restructuring will hit the networking-equipment company with up to $1 billion in severance and other costs. In its most recent annual report, \uc2 Cisco\uc2  reported having 84,900 employees as of July 29, 2023.\par \par \uc2 Cisco\uc2  disclosed the looming job cuts as it reported better-than-expected results for its fiscal fourth-quarter. Revenue, which fell 10%, came in ahead of expectations. The company also issued guidance that met Wall Street views.\par \par \uc2 Shares were up 5.8% in after-hours trading to $48.08. The stock has been down 10% this year.\par \par \uc2 Chief Executive \uc2 Chuck Robbins\uc2  said \uc2 Cisco\uc2  saw steady customer demand with order growth coming across its business "as customers rely on \uc2 Cisco\uc2  to connect and protect all aspects of their organizations in the era of AI."\par \par \uc2 Revenue of $13.64 billion was ahead of the $13.53 billion expected by analysts, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Adjusted earnings came in at 87 cents a share compared with estimates of 85 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 Cisco\uc2  expects revenue between $13.65 billion and $13.85 billion as well as adjusted earnings per share in the range of 86 cents to 88 cents in the current quarter. Analysts polled by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  expected revenue of $13.74 billion and adjusted earnings of 85 cents a share.\par \par \uc2 For fiscal 2025, \uc2 Cisco\uc2  forecast revenue between $55 billion and $56.2 billion as well as adjusted earnings per share in the range of $3.52 to $3.58. Analysts polled by \uc2 FactSet\uc2  expected $55.58 billion in revenue and $3.54 a share in adjusted earnings.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich340\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal5100
