\par\par \b \uc2 Paramount to Close Its TV Studio --- Move comes as entertainment giant begins cutting 15% of its U.S. workforce\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joe Flint \par \uc2 423 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  is restructuring its TV-production business as part of a cost-cutting effort and what the company said were significant changes in the TV and streaming marketplaces.\par \par \uc2 Paramount on Tuesday said that Paramount Television Studios would shut down at the end of the week, and that its sister TV unit -- \uc2 CBS Studios\uc2  -- would absorb the production of Paramount shows as a result of the move. \uc2 CBS Studios\uc2  produces content for the CBS network, Paramount+ and other platforms.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Paramount has been one of the pre-eminent producers of television shows, and Paramount Television Studios recently produced several hits for streaming services including "13 Reasons Why" for \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , "Reacher" for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Prime Video and "Defending Jacob" for Apple TV+. Over the past several years, however, the studio has shrunk in size and status -- a victim of industry consolidation and challenges facing its parent company.\par \par \uc2 The move is part of a shake-up at \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  that will result in about 15% of its U.S. workforce being eliminated, or a cut of approximately 2,000 jobs. \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  parent \uc2 National Amusements\uc2  is being acquired by \uc2 Skydance Media\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a memo to staff, Paramount Global Co-Chief Executive \uc2 George Cheeks\uc2  said the decision isn't based on the performance of the studio, but rather is "the result of significant changes in the TV and streaming marketplace and the need to streamline our company."\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  wrote down the value of its cable-TV networks by nearly $6 billion, a day after rival \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2  revised the worth of its own cable business lower by $9.1 billion.\par \par \uc2 For the past six years, the division has been headed by Nicole Clemens, a well-regarded executive who previously held senior positions at FX and Anonymous Content. Clemens is leaving the company as a result of the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 "We've cemented our legacy by shepherding some of the most influential, award-winning, and critically acclaimed shows in the streaming era," Clemens told staff in a memo sent Tuesday. Cheeks said in his memo that "the studio consistently punched above its weight."\par \par \uc2 The original \uc2 Paramount Television\uc2  launched nearly 60 years ago after being merged with Desilu Productions -- founded by Lucille Ball and Desi Arnaz. It became a force in the industry for the next 30 years with shows such as "Star Trek," "The Brady Bunch," "Happy Days" and "Cheers."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240814ek8e0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
